IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgi-name-changes`

-- Tests for sgi-name-changes.l4 (ss 28, 29, 29A). Expected values are written from the text beside each assertion.

§ `s 28(1) and (2): changing the name`

-- (1): arguments: a special resolution; a name the company could be registered under.
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the company may resolve that its name should be changed to the new name` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the company may resolve that its name should be changed to the new name` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(1) the company may resolve that its name should be changed to the new name` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): the Registrar approves: the duty; not approved: the duty does not arise.
#ASSERT `s 28(2) the Registrar must register the company under the new name and issue the notice of incorporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(2) the Registrar must register the company under the new name and issue the notice of incorporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Arguments: the Registrar approves; the notice has been issued; the day it was issued; the date asked.
#ASSERT `s 28(2) the change of name has become effective` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(2) the change of name has become effective` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(2) the change of name has become effective` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 9 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(2) the change of name has become effective` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 11 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(2) the change of name has become effective` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 11 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 28(3) to (3E): a name that must not stand`

-- Arguments: the five grounds (a) to (e); a special resolution; the new name is not one referred to in (a) to (e).
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company may by special resolution change its name` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company may by special resolution change its name` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company may by special resolution change its name` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company may by special resolution change its name` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company may by special resolution change its name` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No ground, or not a special resolution, or the new name is itself one referred to: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company may by special resolution change its name` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company may by special resolution change its name` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company may by special resolution change its name` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The duty: arguments: the name is within (a) to (e); the Registrar has directed; the Minister has annulled the direction.
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company must change its name within 6 weeks after the direction` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company must change its name within 6 weeks after the direction` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company must change its name within 6 weeks after the direction` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company must change its name within 6 weeks after the direction` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The last day: 6 weeks after 1 March 2026 is 12 April 2026 (P1); a longer period replaces it only if it is longer.
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the last day for compliance` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS Date 12 4 2026
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the last day for compliance` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) EQUALS Date 30 4 2026
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the last day for compliance` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 5 4 2026) EQUALS Date 12 4 2026
-- Arguments: the day of the direction; a longer period allowed; its last day; the company has changed its name; the day it did; the date asked.
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company has complied with the direction` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 12 4 2026) (Date 20 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company has complied with the direction` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 13 4 2026) (Date 20 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company has complied with the direction` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) TRUE (Date 25 4 2026) (Date 26 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company has complied with the direction` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 13 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company has complied with the direction` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 12 4 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company has complied with the direction` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 30 4 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the company has complied with the direction` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The regulative rule, 42 days from the direction: an act on day 42 is in time, on day 43 it is not.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 28(3) the company must change its name within 6 weeks of the direction` "Acme Pte. Ltd." 42 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte. Ltd." DOES `s 28(3) change the company's name as the Registrar has directed` AT 42
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 28(3) the company must change its name within 6 weeks of the direction` "Acme Pte. Ltd." 42 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte. Ltd." DOES `s 28(3) change the company's name as the Registrar has directed` AT 43
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 28(3) the company must change its name within 6 weeks of the direction` "Acme Pte. Ltd." 42 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 43)
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 28(3) the company must change its name within 6 weeks of the direction` "Acme Pte. Ltd." 42 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 42)

-- (3AA): the bar on the ground in section 27(1)(c).
#ASSERT `s 28(3AA) the Registrar is barred from directing a change of name under subsection (3) on the ground` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3AA) the Registrar is barred from directing a change of name under subsection (3) on the ground` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3A): in writing and on a ground in subsection (3).
#ASSERT `s 28(3A) the person may apply to the Registrar for a direction to the company` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3A) the person may apply to the Registrar for a direction to the company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(3A) the person may apply to the Registrar for a direction to the company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The 12-month bar on ground (3)(d): name changed on 1 March 2026, 12 months run to 1 March 2027.
#ASSERT `s 28(3A) the Registrar is barred from considering the application` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3A) the Registrar is barred from considering the application` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(3A) the Registrar is barred from considering the application` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3B): the offence.
#ASSERT `s 28(3B) the person is guilty of the offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3B) the person is guilty of the offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(3B) the person is guilty of the offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(3B) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 2000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 28(3B) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3D): arguments: the decision; the person is the aggrieved company or applicant; the day the Registrar made the decision; the day the applicant was informed of the refusal; the day of the appeal.
#ASSERT `s 28(3D) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` `s 28(3D)(a) the Registrar's decision under subsection (3)` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 9 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3D) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` `s 28(3D)(a) the Registrar's decision under subsection (3)` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 10 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(3D) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` `s 28(3D)(b) the Registrar's refusal to give a direction to a company under subsection (3) pursuant to an application under subsection (3A)` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 9 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3D) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` `s 28(3D)(b) the Registrar's refusal to give a direction to a company under subsection (3) pursuant to an application under subsection (3A)` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(3D) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` `s 28(3D)(a) the Registrar's decision under subsection (3)` FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 9 4 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(3D) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` `s 28(3D) another decision` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 9 4 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(3D) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` `s 28(3D)(a) the Registrar's decision under subsection (3)` TRUE (Date 2 1 2016) (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 3 1 2016) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(3D) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` `s 28(3D)(a) the Registrar's decision under subsection (3)` TRUE (Date 3 1 2016) (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 2 2 2016) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3DA) the decision of the Minister on the appeal is final` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3DA) the decision of the Minister on the appeal is final` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(3E) the Registrar or the Minister must accept as correct the decision of the Court to grant the injunction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3E) the Registrar or the Minister must accept as correct the decision of the Court to grant the injunction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(3E) the Registrar or the Minister must accept as correct the decision of the Court to grant the injunction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 28(4) to (6)`

-- (4): arguments: incorporated under a previous law; the name unchanged since 29 December 1967; the Minister has approved.
#ASSERT `s 28(4) the Registrar is barred from directing the company to change its name under subsection (3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(4) the Registrar is barred from directing the company to change its name under subsection (3)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(4) the Registrar is barred from directing the company to change its name under subsection (3)` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(4) the Registrar is barred from directing the company to change its name under subsection (3)` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5): upon the application and payment of the fee.
#ASSERT `s 28(5) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the incorporation under the new name` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(5) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the incorporation under the new name` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(5) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the incorporation under the new name` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (6): arguments: the name was changed pursuant to this Act; the matter.
#ASSERT `s 28(6) the change of name affects the matter` TRUE `s 28(6) the identity of the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(6) the change of name affects the matter` TRUE `s 28(6) the rights or obligations of the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(6) the change of name affects the matter` TRUE `s 28(6) the validity of legal proceedings by or against the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(6) the change of name affects the matter` TRUE `s 28(6) another matter` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(6) the change of name affects the matter` FALSE `s 28(6) the identity of the company` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(6) the legal proceedings may be continued or commenced by or against the company by its new name` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(6) the legal proceedings may be continued or commenced by or against the company by its new name` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(6) the legal proceedings may be continued or commenced by or against the company by its new name` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 29(1) to (4)`

#ASSERT `s 29(1) the Registrar may approve that the proposed limited company be registered without the word Limited or Berhad` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(1) the Registrar may approve that the proposed limited company be registered without the word Limited or Berhad` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(1) the Registrar may approve that the proposed limited company be registered without the word Limited or Berhad` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(1) the Registrar may approve that the proposed limited company be registered without the word Limited or Berhad` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(1) the Registrar may approve that the proposed limited company be registered without the word Limited or Berhad` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(1) the company may be registered without the word Limited or Berhad accordingly` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(1) the company may be registered without the word Limited or Berhad accordingly` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(2) the Registrar may grant approval to the company to change its name to a name without the word Limited or Berhad` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(2) the Registrar may grant approval to the company to change its name to a name without the word Limited or Berhad` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(2) the Registrar may grant approval to the company to change its name to a name without the word Limited or Berhad` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the conditions are binding on the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the conditions are binding on the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the conditions must be inserted in the constitution of the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the conditions must be inserted in the constitution of the company` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the constitution may be altered by special resolution to give effect to the direction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the constitution may be altered by special resolution to give effect to the direction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(3) the constitution may be altered by special resolution to give effect to the direction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The insertion duty has no time limit, so the s 52 input (the period of all convenient speed, as found) sets the time. The act done in time: FULFILLED. A late act: BREACH. No act: the duty stands (RESIDUAL) until the input runs out.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 29(3) the company must insert the conditions in its constitution if the Registrar so directs` "Acme Pte. Ltd." 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte. Ltd." DOES `s 29(3) insert the conditions in the constitution of the company` AT 5

-- late: the act is done on day 400, past the 7 days the input is, so BREACH
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 29(3) the company must insert the conditions in its constitution if the Registrar so directs` "Acme Pte. Ltd." 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte. Ltd." DOES `s 29(3) insert the conditions in the constitution of the company` AT 400

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 29(3) the company must insert the conditions in its constitution if the Registrar so directs` "Acme Pte. Ltd." 45 AT 0 WITH
-- (4): arguments: a provision requiring the Minister's consent; the Minister has consented; a special resolution.
#ASSERT `s 29(4) the company may alter any provision of the constitution` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(4) the company may alter any provision of the constitution` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(4) the company may alter any provision of the constitution` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(4) the company may alter any provision of the constitution` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 29(5) to (13)`

#ASSERT `s 29(5) the company is exempted from complying with the provisions of this Act relating to the use of the word Limited or Berhad` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(5) the company is exempted from complying with the provisions of this Act relating to the use of the word Limited or Berhad` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (6): arguments: the approval is in force; notice given; an opportunity to be heard afforded.
#ASSERT `s 29(6) the Registrar may revoke the approval` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(6) the Registrar may revoke the approval` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(6) the Registrar may revoke the approval` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(6) the Registrar may revoke the approval` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(6) before the revocation the Registrar must give the company written notice and afford it an opportunity to be heard` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(6) before the revocation the Registrar must give the company written notice and afford it an opportunity to be heard` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(6) upon the revocation the Registrar must enter the word Limited or Berhad at the end of the name in the register` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(6) upon the revocation the Registrar must enter the word Limited or Berhad at the end of the name in the register` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(6) upon the revocation the company ceases to enjoy the exemption` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(6) upon the revocation the company ceases to enjoy the exemption` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(6A) the Registrar may revoke the approval` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(6A) the Registrar may revoke the approval` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(7) the constitution may be altered by special resolution to remove the provision requiring the Minister's consent` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(7) the constitution may be altered by special resolution to remove the provision requiring the Minister's consent` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(7) the constitution may be altered by special resolution to remove the provision requiring the Minister's consent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (8): arguments: the Registrar has approved; the person is the company or the applicant.
#ASSERT `s 29(8) the notice of the approval must be given to the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(8) the notice of the approval must be given to the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(8) the notice of the approval must be given to the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (8A): arguments: the decision; the right person; the day the notice was given; the day of the appeal. 30 days after 10 March 2026 run to 9 April 2026.
#ASSERT `s 29(8A) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` `s 29(8A)(a) the Registrar's decision under subsection (1)` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 9 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(8A) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` `s 29(8A)(a) the Registrar's decision under subsection (1)` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(8A) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` `s 29(8A)(b) the Registrar's decision under subsection (2)` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 9 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(8A) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` `s 29(8A)(b) the Registrar's decision under subsection (2)` FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 9 4 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(8A) the person may appeal to the Minister against the decision` `s 29(8A) another decision` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 9 4 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (9): upon the application and payment of the fee.
#ASSERT `s 29(9) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the approval` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(9) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the approval` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(9) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the approval` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (10): arguments: the members' liability; the 2 years of section 17(6) have expired; registered as a charity.
#ASSERT `s 29(10) section 29 applies to the company` `limited by shares` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(10) section 29 applies to the company` `limited by guarantee` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(10) section 29 applies to the company` `limited by shares` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(10) section 29 applies to the company` `unlimited` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (11) to (13): arguments: the approval, condition or reference was in force immediately before 3 January 2016; the date asked.
#ASSERT `s 29(11) the approval or condition is treated as the Registrar's approval and condition` TRUE (Date 3 1 2016) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(11) the approval or condition is treated as the Registrar's approval and condition` TRUE (Date 2 1 2016) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(11) the approval or condition is treated as the Registrar's approval and condition` FALSE (Date 3 1 2016) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(12) the reference to the Minister's approval is read as a reference to the Registrar` TRUE (Date 3 1 2016) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(12) the reference to the Minister's approval is read as a reference to the Registrar` TRUE (Date 2 1 2016) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(12) the reference to the Minister's approval is read as a reference to the Registrar` FALSE (Date 3 1 2016) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(13) the reference to a direction of the Minister is read as a direction of the Registrar` TRUE (Date 3 1 2016) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(13) the reference to a direction of the Minister is read as a direction of the Registrar` TRUE (Date 2 1 2016) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(13) the reference to a direction of the Minister is read as a direction of the Registrar` FALSE (Date 3 1 2016) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 29A`

